# Raw scrape output — large (~16 MB) and regenerable via scripts/scrape.py.
# The published page uses the normalized data.json instead.
data/*.csv
data/*.db
data/scrape_state.txt

# data/scrape_meta.json is deliberately NOT ignored — it is two lines of
# provenance behind the "Last updated" line on the page.

# Resume state for the long scrapes — meaningful only alongside the (ignored)
# CSVs they track. What they imply about coverage is baked into data.json's
# meta.incomplete at build time, so the published page carries it regardless.
# Full-scrape checkpoints are tracked on purpose, unlike everything else in
# data/. They are ~11 KB, change only when a full scrape runs, and the page
# makes a public claim from them -- which entities are "still being collected".
# When the build moved into CI they were left behind on the laptop, and the
# site spent a day telling readers all 101 entities were half-collected.
# Versioned with the code that reads them, that cannot happen quietly.
data/*_scrape_progress*.json.tmp

# --daily's own within-run resumption and the weekly diff accumulator it
# feeds -- both are transient working state (round-tripped via the GitHub
# Actions cache, not git), same category as the progress files above.
data/*_daily_progress.json*

# The amendment log. Append-only, grows slowly, and is the one file here that
# cannot be regenerated from anything -- a night not recorded is a night gone.
# Gitignored like the rest of data/, so it rides in the Actions cache and must
# go onto the extraction Release with doc_text.jsonl.
data/changes.jsonl
data/daily_diff_report.json

# Working output of scripts/extract_text.py — an append-only checkpoint log
# that grows as documents are processed, not something to commit while
# prototyping.
data/doc_text.jsonl

# scripts/extract_scope.py's output — derived entirely from the file above and
# regenerated in seconds, so it travels with it rather than into git. What
# eventually gets published is a column in the payload, not this.
data/scope.jsonl
# ...and any scratch variant of it. A trial run written to scope.new.jsonl was
# 154 MB, slipped past `git add -A`, and GitHub rejected the push for it after
# the commit was already made. Match the shape, not the one name.
data/scope*.jsonl
data/*.new.jsonl

# prototype-search/ was retired in Aug 2026 (see README.md, "Open work") -- the
# chunked index is no longer published. search.sqlite stays ignored because the
# local copy is still on disk and regenerable from data/doc_text.jsonl, and it
# must never be committed: it is 503 MB.
prototype-search/

# Python
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS
.DS_Store

# The published payload. Built by .github/workflows/pages.yml and deployed as a
# Pages artifact, never committed -- ~100 MB per build entered git history
# permanently under the old branch-publishing setup, and .git reached 546 MB.
# Build locally with scripts/build_site.py to preview; the result stays local.
d/
manifest.json
